<title>HONG KONG: Group Sense year net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Group Sense year net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   6.2 gain     vs 2.7 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  12.15 gain   vs 2.13 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    60.50 profit vs 24.40 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     729.34	 vs 533.89</p>
<p>    Company name		 Group Sense (International) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 11-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 19</p>
<p>NOTE - Group Sense is a consumer electronic manufacturer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$15.66 million on disposal of certain leasehold properties and loss of HK$3.51 million on provision for permanent diminution in value of investment in shares listed overseas.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is three H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
